# Sentinel UI Style

Declared September 10, 2026 after the Week 13 UI audit and nine mockup rounds
(`web/test-results/mockups/overview-v9.html` is the approved reference). This
is the project-declared style under Owen's `my-ui-standard` skill; that skill's
composition principles (emphasis budget, layout follows the job, alignment)
still apply and win over anything here.

## Style: cream canvas, one framed ticket, quiet panels

- **Canvas** is cream `#fff2e9` (sampled from the reference apps). Panels are
  white. That contrast is what makes panels read as objects, so never put a
  white floor behind white panels.
- **The ticket is the one loud element.** The current task (or the pending
  proposal) is a blue `#88aaee` "authorization ticket": 2px black frame,
  6px hard offset shadow, half-circle notches punched into both sides with the
  frame tracing the U. Nothing else on a page has a shadow or a coloured fill.
  Two tickets, or a ticket plus a raised button outside it, is a bug.
- **Panels** (`Panel`) are white, 1.5px black border, 12px radius, no shadow.
  They hold genuinely separate objects: the enforcement grid, the decision
  log, a form, a dialog. Rows live inside panels; a panel never wraps the page.
- **Structure lines** are 1.5px black (sidebar edge, header edge, panel
  borders). Hairlines inside panels are `--line` (warm grey). No other border
  weights.
- **Colour is signal only** outside the ticket: 6px dots in green / amber /
  red / black for ok / warn / off / neutral. No tinted badges, no tinted icon
  tiles, no accent eyebrows.
- **Buttons:** raised (`variant="raised"`: white, 2px black, 3px offset
  shadow) is for the single action inside the ticket. Everything else is
  `secondary` (1px outline) or a quiet text link with the blue underline draw.
- **Type:** Geist (via `next/font/google`) and Geist Mono. Five sizes: 10–11px
  eyebrow (uppercase, +0.08–0.12em), 12px meta, 13px body, 14px emphasis,
  24px ticket title (−0.03em). Weights 400/500/600. IDs, tool names, times,
  and chips in mono.
- **Icons:** Lucide, 15–16px, stroke 1.5–1.6, no containers.
- **Motion:** none decorative. Raised button presses down on hover/active;
  colour transitions 120–180ms; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`.

## Composition by page

- **Overview** is two columns (~68/32 on desktop). Left: eyebrow + workspace
  name, the ticket, then "Enforcement" as a 2×2 panel. Right: "Recent
  decisions" as a vertical log panel. Both column headers are the same height
  and both columns end on the same line: the left column sets the height, the
  log fills it and scrolls internally. Attention (a waiting write) lives in
  the ticket footer, not as a separate strip.
- **Settings** is grouped sections: left section nav, then title → one line →
  rows separated by hairlines inside one white panel per group. No page hero.
- **Tasks** is two columns: the form panel on the left (goal, then two open
  groups, then a collapsed "Advanced"), the same `ContractTicket` on the right
  mirroring the form live (white while draft/ready, blue once active). The one
  raised action is "Confirm task settings" at the form foot while drafting,
  then "Activate task" inside the ticket once confirmed. The activation
  receipt is the same ticket geometry, never a plain dialog. Allowed changes
  is never a field: it is always the chosen operation.
  The page is one screen tall: the form panel scrolls inside with its footer
  pinned, and both columns end on the same line. Before anything is drafted
  the panel is filled with the three steps, not left blank under the goal box.
  A half-filled draft survives switching tabs (kept per browser tab); a
  confirmed copy comes back as an unlocked draft, never as "Ready", because
  the server-side copy may no longer exist.
  Motion is reserved for the one moment authority changes: on activation the
  ticket paints blue left to right, then the receipt rises; both honour
  reduced motion. Nothing else on the page animates.
- **Approvals / Activity:** master-detail. List panel (rows separated by
  hairlines, one dot per row for state) beside a detail panel; both end on
  the same line and scroll internally. With nothing to show, one `Empty`
  panel fills the space instead of a short strip.
- Pickers over typing: where the server knows the valid values (workspace
  paths, fixture issue IDs, the fixed environment) offer them; still let the
  user type, and normalise what they type rather than rejecting it later.
- Context lives in one place. No persistent banner restating the empty state;
  regions with nothing to say are not rendered.
- Use the primitives in `web/src/components/ui/ticket.tsx` (`Ticket`,
  `TicketFacts`, `Chip`) and `web/src/components/ui/layout.tsx` (`Eyebrow`,
  `PageHeader`, `SectionHeader`, `Panel`, `StatusDot`, `KeyValueList`); do not
  hand-roll ticket or panel chrome in pages.

❌ White page with white panels; a raised shadow on every button; a tinted
badge per status; the task in a plain bordered card; a log that runs to the
viewport while the panel beside it stops short.
✅ Cream page, one blue punched ticket with the single raised action inside
it, white 1.5px-black panels for enforcement and the log, both ending on the
same line, colour only in 6px dots.
